# ManhwaManiacs — pull the newest CI-built iOS .ipa so SideStore can offer it
# as an over-the-air update, closing the loop from `git push` to a badge on the
# phone. See ops/fetch-ios-build.sh and .github/workflows/ios-build.yml.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -m 644 ops/manhwamaniacs-ios-sync.cron \
#        /etc/cron.d/manhwamaniacs-ios-sync
# (the installed filename must not contain a dot, or cron ignores it)
#
# Runs as root because the publish directory under /srv/apps is owned by nas,
# and the script chowns the published .ipa to the container's uid.
#
# No credentials needed: builds are published as release assets on a public
# repo, which are anonymously downloadable. (Workflow *artifacts* are not —
# GitHub demands auth for those even on a public repo, which is why the release
# path exists.) If the repo ever goes private again, the script falls back to
# the artifact API and will then need a token with Actions:read at
# /root/.gh_token. See ops/fetch-ios-build.sh.
#
# Every 10 minutes: an iOS build takes ~5 min, so this adds at most a few
# minutes on top of the build itself. Runs with nothing new cost one API call.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

*/10 * * * * root /apps/dev/aistudio/ops/ios-sync-cron.sh
